1. Introduction
Welcome to [Your App Name] ("we," "our," or "us"). We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting the personal data you share with us. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, process, and safeguard your information when you use our automated TikTok video creation and scheduled publishing application (the "App").
2. Information We Collect
To provide automated publishing and media processing services, we collect the following categories of data:
A. Account & Contact Data
Name, email address, and authentication details when you register for an account.
Subscription and billing information processed securely via third-party payment providers (e.g., Stripe). We do not directly store credit card numbers.
B. TikTok Data (via TikTok API / OAuth)
When you connect your TikTok account to the App using TikTok OAuth authorization, we access and store:
Account Identifiers: TikTok User ID, username, profile picture, and display name.
OAuth Tokens: Access tokens and refresh tokens required to upload and publish content to your account automatically on your behalf.
Publishing Status & Video Metrics: Metadata related to posts submitted through our App (e.g., upload status, video IDs).
C. User-Provided Content & Assets
Videos, images, audio files, captions, scripts, and media metadata uploaded or generated within the App for processing, editing, or automated posting.
D. Technical & Usage Data
Log data including IP address, browser/device type, operating system, timestamp of requests, system performance logs, and feature usage statistics.
3. How We Use Your Information
We use collected data solely to deliver and optimize our automation platform:
Core Functionality: To edit, process, render, schedule, and automatically upload video content to your linked TikTok account via official APIs.
Account Management: To manage subscriptions, authenticate users, and provide customer support.
System Maintenance: To monitor system health, fix bugs, prevent abuse, and enforce API rate limits.
Legal Compliance: To comply with legal obligations and enforce our Terms of Service.
4. How We Share & Disclose Information
We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We only share data under the following circumstances:
Third-Party APIs (TikTok): Video uploads, account linking, and API calls require transmission of data to TikTok (ByteDance Ltd.) in accordance with TikTok's Privacy Policy.
Service Providers: Cloud hosting infrastructure (e.g., AWS, GCP), storage providers, and payment processors who operate under strict data privacy obligations.
Legal Requirements: If required by law, subpoena, or governmental regulation to protect our rights or user safety.
5. Data Retention & Account Disconnection
OAuth Tokens: You can revoke our App's access to your TikTok account at any time via your TikTok Security Settings or within our App dashboard. Revoking access permanently invalidates stored access tokens.
Uploaded Media: Media files stored on our servers for automated queuing are deleted after processing or in accordance with your specified retention settings.
Account Deletion: You may request full account and data deletion by contacting us at [Your Contact Email].
6. Security
We implement industry-standard administrative, physical, and technical security measures (including TLS encryption in transit and AES encryption at rest for sensitive tokens) to protect your personal information against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration.
7. Children's Privacy
Our App is not intended for individuals under the age of 18 (or the age of digital consent in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
